import html
p=Path(__file__).parent
sql=(p/'migrations/002_family_workflow.sql').read_text()
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>GameTrace — Family setup update</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#101410;color:#edf2ed;font:16px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:650px;margin:auto;padding:28px 22px}h1{font-size:28px;line-height:1.2}a{color:#20d476}button{width:100%;min-height:48px;padding:12px;border:1px solid #20d476;border-radius:12px;background:#19241b;color:#fff;font:inherit}textarea{box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:220px;margin:16px 0;background:#0c100c;color:#d7ded7;border:1px solid #475247;border-radius:8px;padding:12px;font:12px/1.5 monospace}li{margin:14px 0}.note{border:1px solid #475247;border-radius:12px;padding:16px}#status{color:#20d476}label{display:block}</style><main><a href="/">← GameTrace</a><h1>Update Family Cloud</h1><p>One setup update for your existing GameTrace Supabase project.</p><p class="note">This preserves families, games, training and recordings. Each family creator becomes its Owner. Existing invitation codes expire; Owners and Admins can generate new 7-day codes afterward.</p><ol><li>Tap <strong>Copy setup SQL</strong> below.</li><li>In Supabase, open <strong>GameTrace → SQL Editor → New query</strong>. Paste the complete SQL and tap <strong>Run</strong>. You should see “Success. No rows returned.”</li><li>In <strong>Authentication → URL Configuration</strong>, allow this development redirect: <code>https://development--game-trace.netlify.app/?family_auth=1</code>. This lets confirmation and password-reset emails return to GameTrace.</li><li>Refresh GameTrace, open Family Cloud, and tap <strong>Check family connection</strong> or <strong>Sync now</strong>.</li></ol><button id="copy">Copy setup SQL</button><p id="status" role="status"></p><details><summary>Show SQL / manual copy</summary><label for="sql">Complete family workflow migration</label><textarea id="sql" readonly spellcheck="false">'''+html.escape(sql)+'''</textarea></details><p>If iPhone copying is blocked, expand “Show SQL,” tap the text, then Select All → Copy. In the SQL Editor, use the iPhone three-finger paste gesture if long-press paste does not appear.</p><p>This update belongs in the existing project; do not run the original schema again.</p><script>document.getElementById('copy').onclick=async()=>{const text=document.getElementById('sql');try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text.value);document.getElementById('status').textContent='Copied. Paste into a new Supabase SQL query.'}catch{document.querySelector('details').open=true;text.focus();text.select();document.getElementById('status').textContent='SQL selected. Use Select All → Copy.'}};</script></main></html>'''
